theory.intro:
The graph of $y = f^{-1}(x)$ is the reflection of the graph of $y = f(x)$ in the line $y = x$. Every point $(a, b)$ on $y = f(x)$ becomes the point $(b, a)$ on $y = f^{-1}(x)$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-3.8,0) -- (4.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.4) -- (0,4.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[dashed] (-3,-3) -- (3.7,3.7);
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-3:2.68, samples=80, smooth, variable=\x] plot ({\x}, {0.5*exp(\x*ln(2)) + 1});
\draw[thick, <->, domain=1.07:4.4, samples=80, smooth, variable=\x] plot ({\x}, {ln(2*(\x - 1))/ln(2)});
\fill (2,3) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (3,2) circle (2.5pt);
\node at (1.2,3.35) {$(a,b)$};
\node at (3.6,1.4) {$(b,a)$};
\node at (-1.6,3.4) {$y=f(x)$};
\node at (2.8,-1.6) {$y=f^{-1}(x)$};
\node at (-2.9,-1.6) {$y=x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
The curve $y = 2^x - 1$ passes through $(0, 0)$, $(1, 1)$, and $(2, 3)$ with horizontal asymptote $y = -1$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.6]
\draw[->] (-3,0) -- (4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3) -- (0,4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[dashed, gray] (-2.5,-2.5) -- (3.5,3.5) node[above right] {$y=x$};
\draw[dashed, red] (-3,-1) -- (4,-1) node[below left] {$y=-1$};
\draw[thick, blue, domain=-2.8:2.2, samples=60] plot (\x, {exp(\x*ln(2)) - 1});
\fill[blue] (0,0) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$(0,0)$};
\fill[blue] (1,1) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$(1,1)$};
\fill[blue] (2,3) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$(2,3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
State the asymptote and key points for the graph of $y = f^{-1}(x)$.

development.solution_text:
$\text{Vertical asymptote: } x = -1$
$\text{Reflected points: } (0, 0), (1, 1), (3, 2)$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.6]
\draw[->] (-3,0) -- (4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3) -- (0,4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[dashed, gray] (-2.5,-2.5) -- (3.5,3.5) node[above right] {$y=x$};
\draw[dashed, red] (-1,-3) -- (-1,4) node[above left] {$x=-1$};
\draw[thick, teal, domain=-0.85:3.5, samples=60] plot (\x, {ln(\x + 1)/ln(2)});
\fill[teal] (0,0) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$(0,0)$};
\fill[teal] (1,1) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$(1,1)$};
\fill[teal] (3,2) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$(3,2)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
